## Technical Implementation

The following code excerpts are taken directly from the production codebase and represent the complete set of `message.content` access points.

### The Command Gate (`bot.js`)

This is the only location where `message.content` is read to classify a message as a command or ambient chat.

```js
const isCommand = message.content.startsWith(prefix) &&
  message.content.length > prefix.length &&
  message.content[prefix.length] !== ' ';

if (!isCommand) {
  utils.scheduleSpawnForChannel(message.channel, message.author.id).catch(() => {});
  return;
}

const args = message.content.slice(prefix.length).trim().split(/ +/);
const command = args.shift().toLowerCase();
// message.content is not referenced again after this point
```

Five and only five operations are performed on `message.content` in the entire codebase:

1. `.trim()` to check for a bare bot @mention and reply with the current server prefix
2. `.startsWith(prefix)` to detect command intent
3. `.length > prefix.length` to reject bare prefix input
4. `[prefix.length] !== ' '` to reject false positives such as `. hello` vs `.hello`
5. `.slice(prefix.length).trim().split(/ +/)` to extract the command name and arguments

No other file in the codebase reads `message.content`.

### Spawn Scheduling (`src/utils/scheduleSpawnForChannel.js`)

```js
async function scheduleSpawnForChannel(channel, triggerUserId = null) {
  if (!channel.guild) return; // DMs excluded entirely
  const timeSinceLastSpawn = now - lastSpawn;
  let requiredCooldown = global.SPAWN_COOLDOWN_MS || 120000; // Default 2 minutes
  if (timeSinceLastSpawn >= requiredCooldown) {
    await createSpawn(targetChannel, null, null, null, triggerUserId);
  }
}
```

Spawns are guild-only, channel-specific, and cooldown-gated. The triggering user's ID is used only to check their favorites list for a spawn bias roll (a single database read: `SELECT guest_id FROM user_favorites WHERE user_id = $1 LIMIT 1`). The user's message activity is not recorded.

### Claim Name Matching (`src/commands/claim.js`)

```js
const userInput = args.join(' ');
const reversedInput = [...args].reverse().join(' ');
const normalize = s => s.replace(/[^a-zA-Z\s]/g, '').toLowerCase();
const spawnNameNorm = normalize(channelSpawn.characterName);
const inputNorm = normalize(userInput);
const distance = levenshteinDistance(inputNorm, spawnNameNorm);
if (distance === 1) return message.reply({ content: 'Incorrect name, you are 1 letter off.' });
```

### Client Configuration and Cache Limits (`bot.js`)

```js
const client = new Client({
  intents: [
    GatewayIntentBits.Guilds,
    GatewayIntentBits.GuildMessages,
    GatewayIntentBits.MessageContent,
    GatewayIntentBits.DirectMessages,
    GatewayIntentBits.GuildMembers,
  ],
  makeCache: Options.cacheWithLimits({
    MessageManager: 100,  // Hard limit: max 100 messages cached per channel
    ReactionManager: 0,   // Reactions not cached at all
  }),
  sweepers: {
    messages: {
      interval: 300,   // Sweep every 5 minutes
      lifetime: 600,   // Purge messages older than 10 minutes
    },
  },
});
```

The message cache is hard-limited to 100 messages per channel. Reactions are not cached. Cache sweeping runs every 5 minutes and purges messages older than 10 minutes.

### `messageDelete` Handler Does Not Read Content (`bot.js`)

```js
client.on('messageDelete', async (message) => {
  const channelSpawn = settings.channelSpawns[message.channel.id];
  if (channelSpawn && channelSpawn.messageId === message.id) {
    delete settings.channelSpawns[message.channel.id];
  }
});
```

The delete handler checks only `message.id` to clean up spawn state when a moderator removes a spawn embed. `message.content` is not accessed.

