## Privacy Controls

**Channel restriction.** The spawn system activates only in channels explicitly designated by server administrators via `.setspawnchannel`. Messages in all other channels are processed identically (prefix check only) with no spawn scheduling or recording.

**Server blacklist.** A full server blacklist is maintained. Blacklisted servers receive no responses from the bot.

**Message cache limits.** The message cache is hard-limited to 100 messages per channel with automatic sweeping every 5 minutes and a 10-minute maximum message lifetime.

**No DM monitoring.** The spawn system explicitly exits early for DM channels (`if (!channel.guild) return`). The bot does not monitor DMs unless a user directly addresses it.

**Account deletion.** Users can request complete data deletion through the Eroth support server. Deletion removes all records across every table keyed to the user's Discord ID: profile, characters, guild membership, trade history, reminders, wishlist, favorites, tags, titles, dungeon history, gear, and all related records.

**Database encryption.** The PostgreSQL database is hosted on Railway with encrypted storage volumes at rest.
